  'fire-fire': "Your Sun and Moon both burn with fire, so what you want and what you feel tend to arrive together, and loudly. You run on enthusiasm, and one idea from you can get a whole group out of their chairs. The risk is burning out, since you rarely stop to refuel. Build in real downtime, like a phone free Sunday morning, and finish one project before you chase the next bright spark that catches your eye.",
  'fire-earth': "Fire and earth together give you a spark and a plan. One part of you wants to leap, while the other wants to check the budget first. That mix can make you an excellent builder of dreams, as long as each side gets a say. When an idea excites you, write down the first practical step before you act, and when caution keeps you frozen, set a start date and keep it like an appointment.",
  'fire-air': "Fire and air feed each other, so your heart and your mind both love movement and new ideas. You can be inspiring company and a great starter of plans, the friend who suggests the road trip at midnight. The challenge is grounding all that energy. Choose one idea each month to carry through to the end, and keep a calendar where you can see your promises, so your spark comes with steady follow through.",
  'fire-water': "Fire and water make a rich, steamy mix of strong drive and deep feeling. You want to act boldly, yet your emotions run deep and can pull you another way. This gives you real passion and real empathy at once. When the two clash, pause and ask what your heart needs before you charge ahead, and give your feelings an active outlet, like dancing in the living room or a long swim at the pool.",
  'earth-earth': "With both lights in earth, you are practical and grounded through and through. You trust what you can see and touch, and people rely on you to get things done well. The risk is getting stuck in routine or worrying too much about security. Add a little play to your week, like a new recipe or a day trip to a town you have never visited, so life keeps some fresh air and surprise.",
  'earth-air': "Earth and air pair a practical streak with a curious mind. You like to think things through and then make them real, which can make you a strong planner at work and the person friends call when something needs sorting out. Sometimes your head races while your body wants to rest. Balance the two by turning each idea into a small, concrete task you can finish in a single afternoon.",
  'earth-water': "Earth and water make a fertile, nurturing mix. You care deeply and show it through practical support, like cooking for a sick friend or fixing a neighbor's fence. You value security and closeness, and you build bonds that last for decades. Watch for a habit of holding on too tight to people or routines. Letting a little change in from time to time keeps your inner garden growing and green.",
